Rules:
  [A1] Use standalone components (Angular 14+).
  [A2] Use TypeScript strict mode.
  [A3] Use `@Input` and `@Output` for component communication.
  [A4] Use services for business logic.
  [A5] Use `*ngIf`, `*ngFor`, `*ngSwitch` for structural directives.
  [A6] Use `{{ }}` interpolation for text content.
  [A7] Use `[property]` binding for DOM properties.
  [A8] Use `(event)` binding for DOM events.

Pros:
  - Full-featured framework
  - Strong typing
  - Enterprise support

Cons:
  - Steep learning curve
  - Verbose boilerplate
  - Heavy bundle size

Alternatives:
  - React
  - Vue
  - Svelte

State: +

